menu "DAC user interface"

    choice UI_PANEL
        prompt "TFT panel controller"
        default UI_PANEL_ILI9341
        help
            Which controller the 2.4" SPI module uses. ILI9341 is by far the
            most common; ST7789 shows up on some 240x320 modules. If the display
            stays blank or the colours are inverted, this is the first thing to
            check -- the modules are not visually distinguishable.

        config UI_PANEL_ILI9341
            bool "ILI9341"

        config UI_PANEL_ST7789
            bool "ST7789"
    endchoice

    config UI_PANEL_INVERT_COLOR
        bool "Invert panel colours"
        default n
        help
            Some panels ship with inverted colour polarity. Symptom is a
            photographic negative, not a blank screen.

    config UI_LVGL_BUFFER_LINES
        int "LVGL draw buffer height (lines)"
        default 40
        range 10 320
        help
            Two buffers of this many lines are allocated in internal DMA-capable
            RAM. At 240px wide and 16bpp that is 480 bytes per line per buffer,
            so 40 lines costs about 38 KB for the pair.

            This is the first dial to turn if the ESP32-WROOM-32 runs out of
            internal RAM once Bluetooth connects: dropping to 20 lines halves
            it, at the cost of more, smaller SPI transfers.

endmenu
